[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579121802","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101323#issuecomment-2579121802","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101323","id":2579121802,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZukaK","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T03:42:36Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T03:42:36Z","body":"This *does* fix the issue, but part of that initial change was to make us less reliant on including `modules_enabled.gen.h` in headers. This should be fine to merge still, as that idea is ultimately going to be more thoroughly enforced by #100023","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579121802/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579497910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101323#issuecomment-2579497910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101323","id":2579497910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZwAO2","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T08:59:29Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T09:01:04Z","body":"I updated the commit to be more precise:\r\n- The module wasn't disabled, it's just the configuration warning which was wrongly shown. Baking and using lightmaps would actually still work, this was just a warning bug.\r\n- `MODULE_LIGHTMAPPER_RD_ENABLED` is only checked in `lightmap_gi.cpp`, so that's where `modules_enabled.gen.h` should be included. This should always be exactly where it's used (to the point of being duplicated if it's used in both .h and .cpp), specifically to prevent such issues.\r\n- Likewise, all `modules_enabled.gen.h` includes by convention should specify with a comment why they're included, so that we don't make mistakes like this when refactoring. This is something that PR reviewers should watch for, any new code that checks a `MODULE_*_ENABLED` defined should satisfy those two points.","author_associatio